// MacScopeNativeDecompiler/PcodeOpcodeVocabulary.def
//
// Single source of truth for the exported p-code opcode vocabulary.
// MACSCOPE_PCODE_OPCODE(ghidra_enumerator, canonical_export_name, wire_token)
//
// Hand-authored 2026-08-18 and checked against the pinned SLEIGH package by a probe
// that linked ghidra::get_opname() and enumerated the full OpCode range. There is no
// generator script: this file is maintained by hand, and Scripts/tests/
// test_pcode_opcode_vocabulary_parity.py is what keeps the copies honest.
//
// OPEN GAP — no test binds this file to ghidra::OpCode. The parity test compares the
// manifest to the Swift enum and to the C++/ObjC++ expansions, all of which derive
// from this file, so a package repin that renumbers or renames an opcode would pass
// every test in the repository while silently reintroducing MS-01. Closing that needs
// PcodeOpcodeVocabularyBindingTests.cpp links against the pinned package and walks
// CPUI_COPY..<CPUI_MAX, including SPULL and the intentional raw-value hole at 45.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS: ghidra::get_opname() is NOT a safe source for exported names in this
// pinned version. Its name table disagrees with the OpCode enum for 11 opcodes -- the six
// CPUI_FLOAT_* conversions lose their FLOAT_ prefix, and MULTIEQUAL/INDIRECT/PTRADD/PTRSUB
// return the sleigh-compiler tokens BUILD/DELAY_SLOT/LABEL/CROSSBUILD. Nine of those are
// live defects: the wire codec rejects an unrecognised name and fails the WHOLE result.
//
// Rule: canonical name is the enumerator without its CPUI_ prefix; wire token is that
// lowercased. CPUI_ZPULL is the single deliberate exception (exported as EXTRACT/extract).

MACSCOPE_PCODE_OPCODE(CPUI_COPY               , "COPY"              , "copy")
MACSCOPE_PCODE_OPCODE(CPUI_LOAD               , "LOAD"              , "load")
